 ## 中文摘要
 
-为支持并发执行与统一回写，Agent Center将常驻Supervisor与临时executor封装为一个逻辑Agent。本文结合冻结协作记录、历史源码、操作者回顾与受控动作实验，研究这种软件归属为何未自动转化为持续的交付责任。7月22日，两个agent分别将内部执行失败外推为外部阻塞，经用户提醒后修正责任解释；次日，开发者将其概括为身份认知问题并推动提示修订。8月记录同时出现启动责任误归属与正确承责，9月4日仍出现把不合格执行结果视为自身责任终点、再次依赖人工纠正的片段。操作者回顾称问题早期频繁、多次提醒后逐步改善但仍偶发；现有材料支持反复纠偏及后期残留，尚无发生率或改善幅度的可靠分母。另开展两模型共512次合成动作选择、32次默认预期诊断及3次事后续步。在责任与恢复义务已完整显式提供的干净子集中，两模型均64/64首步到达控制边界，单句身份表述的配对差异为0。该结果说明明确协议可以被遵循，不能否定历史责任断裂或证明无需人工校准。线程、工作区与恢复接口故障继续从架构后果归因中排除，训练先验的来源亦未识别。设计上应将执行隔离与目标责任分开，持续关联合法修复、补证和升级路径，并以无提醒恢复及人工干预负担评价封装。全部分析尚未人工复核。（证据A00–A22）
+Agent Center将常驻Supervisor与临时executor封装为同一逻辑Agent，以支持并发执行、任务隔离与统一回写。本文考察这一封装能否维持执行失败后的交付责任，以及人工为何仍需反复纠正责任归属。研究采用单部署的回顾性案例比较，结合原生消息、任务动作、历史提示与两模型受控动作实验，区分执行失败、责任解释、恢复行动和交付结果。案例显示，Supervisor会将自身executor的失败解释为外部阻塞，或在拒绝不合格产物后把任务结束视为交付义务结束；直接提醒和提示修订之后，正确承责与后期再次纠偏仍同时存在。512次合成动作选择中，两模型在明确责任与合法恢复动作的干净条件下均64/64首步到达控制边界，身份表述的配对差为0。这支持明确协议下的动作遵循，却没有检验长期运行中的自主承责。研究结论是：统一的软件身份不足以建立稳定的责任连续性；执行隔离、质量审查与目标责任需要分别表示，并通过合法修复、补证或升级持续连接。人工反复重建这一连接是本部署的实际维护负担。现有证据尚未量化该负担，也未分离抽象、接口与训练先验各自的因果贡献；明显系统故障不计入架构效应。
 
 **关键词：**逻辑 Agent；Supervisor/executor；责任归属；执行生命周期；agent harness
 
 ## Abstract
 
-Agent Center grouped a persistent Supervisor and temporary executors into one logical Agent to support concurrent work and unified writeback. We examine why this software-level ownership did not automatically sustain delivery responsibility, using frozen collaboration records, historical source code, an operator account, and controlled action-selection experiments. On 22 July, two agents treated failures of their own execution units as external blockers and revised their responsibility statements after human reminders. A developer diagnosis and prompt revision followed. August records contain both renewed actor misattribution and appropriate ownership; on 4 September, further episodes treated an inadequate executor result as the endpoint of the agent's responsibility and again prompted human correction. The operator recalls frequent early confusion, gradual improvement after repeated reminders, and occasional later errors. The dated records corroborate repeated correction and later occurrences, but do not establish incidence or improvement rates. Separately, 512 synthetic action selections, 32 incomplete-protocol probes, and three post hoc continuations were conducted across two models. With responsibility and recovery obligations already explicit, both models reached the control boundary in 64/64 clean-condition first actions, with zero paired difference between single-sentence identity framings. This demonstrates protocol-following under those conditions, not the absence of historical responsibility breakdowns or a reduced need for human calibration. Thread, workspace, and recovery-interface faults remain excluded from architectural outcome attribution; training-related causes are unidentified. Design evaluation should distinguish execution isolation from continuing goal ownership and measure authorized recovery without reminders and the burden of human intervention. The analyses have not been human-verified. (Evidence A00–A22)
+Agent Center combines a persistent Supervisor and temporary executors within one logical Agent to support concurrency, isolation, and unified writeback. This study asks whether that abstraction sustains delivery responsibility after execution failures and why repeated human correction remains necessary. A retrospective single-deployment case comparison combines native messages, task actions, historical prompts, and controlled action-selection experiments with two models. The analysis separates execution failure, responsibility attribution, recovery action, and delivery outcome. Supervisors sometimes treated failures of their own executors as external blockers or treated rejection of an inadequate candidate as the end of their delivery obligation. Human reminders and prompt revisions were followed by both appropriate ownership and later episodes requiring correction. Across 512 synthetic action selections, each model reached the control boundary in 64/64 clean-condition actions, with zero paired difference between identity framings. Because responsibility and authorized recovery were explicit in both conditions, these results establish protocol-following within the tested tasks, not sustained autonomous ownership. The central finding is that unified software identity did not reliably preserve responsibility continuity. Execution isolation and quality review must remain connected to authorized repair, evidence collection, or escalation. Repeated human reconstruction of that connection was an observed maintenance burden, although its magnitude and the separate causal roles of abstraction, interfaces, and training priors remain unmeasured. Evident system faults are excluded from architectural outcome attribution.
 
 **Keywords:** logical agent; supervisor/executor; accountability; execution lifecycle; agent harness
 
 ## 1 引言
 
-Agent Center 将常驻 Supervisor 与临时 executor 封装为一个逻辑 Agent，起点是并发执行的工程需求。早期设计中，串行锁位于 Agent 粒度，同一 Agent 只能排队处理任务；中心连接的身份又在进程启动时固定。设计希望在保留长期任务归属的同时，让同一个 Agent 并行处理多个任务，并按任务选择模型。（A14）
-
-这一方案将中心交互与具体执行分开。Supervisor 接收消息、组织上下文、选择模型并启动执行；executor 在独立上下文和工作区中完成单项任务，结束后退出。结果交回 Supervisor，由其统一更新中心和记忆。逻辑 Agent 则继续承载配置、身份和交付责任。唯一写入入口旨在约束并发状态更新，临时执行单元提供任务级隔离，图1展示了这些设计关系。（A14 §2–8；A01）
-
-分离进程以后，模型必须持续维持另一组关系：当前会话负责控制，具体实现发生在其它会话，而失败后的修复、补证和最终交付仍由同一逻辑Agent负责。历史记录显示，这种责任没有随软件封装自然成立。7月22日，两个不同agent分别被用户提醒executor是其自身的一部分；7月23日，开发者进一步要求修订身份与审查提示。后续既有正确承责，也有再次把执行失败当作外部问题、把审查结束当作交付责任结束的片段。本文研究的是这一反复需要人工纠偏的责任断裂，而不只是模型能否复述一个身份定义。（A01–A06、A15、A21）
-
-本文把“身份混淆”限定为行动者、能力和交付责任的误归属，不涉及模型的意识或内在自我。相关研究已有角色规范与协调失败分类。[1]<!--ref:R01--><!--anchor:section:4--> 本文区分现象、机制与净因果：历史材料可以支持责任外推及人工纠正的存在，而抽象、角色提示、恢复接口和模型既有行为模式各自贡献多少仍需辨别。系统bug不能作为架构造成技术故障的证据，但也不能将故障之后可分离的责任解释一并抹去。合成实验仅检验已明确给定责任时的动作遵循，不承担否定生产现象的作用。（A02–A06、A14–A22）
+Agent Center引入Supervisor–Executor分工，是为了解决同一Agent只能串行处理任务、中心连接身份固定以及并发写入难以协调的问题。常驻Supervisor接收消息、组织上下文并统一回写，临时executor在隔离会话与工作区中执行具体任务；配置、身份和交付责任仍归于一个逻辑Agent。这一结构使执行可以分离，但要求交付义务在多个执行单元之间保持连续。（A01、A14）
+
+本文的核心研究问题是：**将Supervisor与executor定义为同一逻辑Agent，为什么仍未稳定维持执行失败后的交付责任？** 这里的“责任连续性”指：一次执行失败或候选被拒绝后，只要目标尚未完成或获授权终止，当前负责者仍将剩余工作连接到合法的修复、补证、交接或升级。它不要求Supervisor亲自写代码，也不要求越权重开任务或无限重试。进程不同是正常隔离；把进程不同进一步理解为“其失败不再由我负责”，才是本文所研究的责任外置。
+
+这一问题在运行中有直接表现：Supervisor能够发现不合格产物，却以外部评审者自居；也能识别没有executor在工作，却把启动责任留给中心。用户反复提醒executor属于当前Agent，并推动身份与审查提示修订。后续出现正确承责，也再次需要纠偏。本文据此研究责任在哪个环节中断、人工补充了什么，以及明确责任之后模型是否仍会选错动作。（A02–A06、A10、A15、A21）
+
+本研究将软件身份、行为责任和因果解释分开。已有多Agent失败分类讨论角色规范与协调错位，[1]<!--ref:R01--><!--anchor:section:4--> 本文进一步考察一个逻辑Agent内部的执行分离如何伴随责任外置。历史案例用于识别这一运行问题，短题实验用于检验给定协议下的表示敏感性。二者共同支持对当前封装的设计评价：软件归属没有替代持续的行为责任管理。抽象、恢复接口与模型先验各自的贡献，则属于进一步的因果问题。
 
